cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite the white paper."
title: "fAI: a deterministic question-answering engine that cannot make things up"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kylor"
    given-names: "Soren"
date-released: "2026-09-28"
abstract: >-
  fAI is a deterministic, LLM-free question-answering engine. Every factual
  sentence is quoted word for word from a named source, computed by a
  checkable rule, or filled into a fixed pattern from cited database facts;
  otherwise it abstains. It runs on a Raspberry Pi 4 with 4 GB of memory.
keywords:
  - deterministic question answering
  - LLM-free
  - extractive question answering
  - hallucination
  - retrieval
  - Raspberry Pi
  - Wikidata
  - offline AI
preferred-citation:
